config U30PRO_SPRD_CPUFREQ_V2
 tristate "Unisoc apcpu hardware DVFS cpufreq driver (sprd,cpufreq-v2)"
 depends on ARCH_SPRD && CPU_FREQ && U30PRO_SPRD_SIP
 select PM_OPP
 help
   Scales the voltage and frequency of the two CPU clusters through the hardware DVFS of the secure monitor (SIP SMC calls).  The
   driver only starts when the kernel command line contains u30pro_cpufreq=1.  ASE aging compensation (u30pro_ase=1) and the data for the
   software SCU frequency control (u30pro_scufreq=1, see U30PRO_SPRD_SCUFREQ) are optional; the debugfs table is ported read-only.
